# [DD-13b.W23.3] DECISION 3's FALSIFICATION POINT (§2.27.2, RULED at
# r58): inside an OPEN SUBTREE a trimmed bare `|` is the LITERAL byte `|`
# and opens nothing.
#
# This is the one production whose key space pcrec does not control, so a
# literal `|` has to stay writable there — and S3 opening a prose region
# would take it away silently. The two assertions are separate on
# purpose: the `separator` row's value is the single byte `|`, AND the
# sibling below it at the SAME indent is a SIBLING ROW rather than a
# continuation. If S3 still opened inside an open subtree, the value
# would be empty and the sibling would have been swallowed — two
# symptoms, and a fixture asserting only "the file is accepted" sees
# neither.
#
# It REPLACES revision 3.4's `aux_prose_value.rxtin`, which asserted the
# opposite; the ruling that removed prose values from aux bodies is what
# inverted it.
pattern a+
ext bench
  separator |
  terminator ;
  note this line is a sibling of both, not a continuation of either
m "aaa" 0 3
